change('.bss','state_behavior','Initialization clears the first 0x24 bytes, preserves x24, and sets the initialized and capture flags. Capture toggling changes x0_b1 and the global callback but leaves x0_b0 set, so history remains readable. Absolute seek walks length trailers while requested rows remain and the prior distance is below capacity; it has no stored-row-count guard and may finish beyond capacity. Sequential line end returns zero and moves toward newer text. Positive relative movement leaves the cached x20 line length unchanged.')
change('fn_80393C14','data_flow','Snapshots capacity, write index, buffer pointer and partial-line length. Ordinary bytes and completed-line length trailers are written modulo capacity; x1C increases for each byte or trailer and x18 for each completed line. These fields also represent the selected cursor history distance and row and are overwritten by seek operations, so they are not independent lifetime totals. The updated write index and partial-line length are committed after scanning the input span.')
