change('hsd_80393DA0','state_behavior','Clears the first 0x24 bytes of the 0x28-byte state, preserving x24; stores and zero-fills the caller buffer, sets both initialized and capture flags, and registers fn_80393C14. There is no allocation or argument validation here. Later capture needs writable storage with positive capacity because character writes use modulo capacity; HSD_LogInit separately installs stdout interception.')
change('hsd_80393E34','data_flow','Copies x14 and x18 into independently optional output pointers without modifying state. The debug address parser saves both values, seeks and reads text, then passes the saved values back to hsd_80393E68. Reconstructing the same position depends on the history not changing during that interval.')
change('hsd_80393E68','purpose','Positions the report-history cursor by walking backward from the current unfinished line through byte-length trailers. It stops when the requested row count is reached or the prior backward distance is at least capacity; it does not validate an oldest complete retained line or consult an available-row count.')
change('hsd_80393E68','state_behavior','Returns unchanged when x0_b0 is clear. Otherwise starts with current partial-line length and walks trailers while counter < row and pos < capacity. Each iteration increments pos, reads a trailer modulo capacity, then adds its length, so the final distance may exceed capacity. Stores counter, distance and selected length and clamps the unsigned column to that length. Negative signed callers convert to unsigned coordinates; no signed-range validation exists.')
change('hsd_80393EF4','data_flow','Reads x0_b0, capacity, write index, buffer, column, row, backward distance and cached line length. Positive row movement follows length trailers backward and stores the new row, distance and adjusted column, but does not store the newly read length into x20. Negative row movement recomputes nonnegative coordinates before calling hsd_80393E68. An initial distance at or beyond capacity delegates directly with summed coordinates, without the negative-branch saturation.')
change('hsd_80393EF4','purpose','Adjusts the report-history read cursor using signed row and column deltas. The positive-row branch traverses older lines and adjusts the column but leaves cached x20 unchanged; the negative-row branch seeks from the current write position. With an in-range saved distance, a zero row delta also ignores a nonzero column delta.')
change('hsd_80393EF4','state_behavior','Returns when uninitialized. A saved distance >= capacity delegates immediately to absolute seek with coordinate sums, so zero-row movement can still act in that branch. Otherwise positive rows walk trailers while the prior distance is below capacity, update row and distance, and clamp horizontal movement using the local destination length without updating x20. Negative rows saturate computed coordinates at zero before absolute seek. Zero rows do nothing in the in-range branch. Extreme signed sums or negations are not guarded.')
change('hsd_80394068','data_flow','Reads the initialized flag x0_b0, capacity, selected backward distance, column, cached line length, write index and backing pointer. For a column below cached length, returns out_buf[(column + write_index + capacity - distance) % capacity] and increments column. Drawing masks the byte with 0x7F for a font index; the address parser consumes successive bytes as hexadecimal digits. Capture-enable x0_b1 does not gate this read.')
change('hsd_80394068','inferred_type','Signature u8 (void). Returns a stored byte or zero for uninitialized state, an excessive history distance or line end. Stored NUL bytes are also possible because the capture callback accepts arbitrary non-CR/non-LF bytes, so zero is not a unique error sentinel.')
change('hsd_80394068','purpose','Reads a byte at the shared report-history cursor and advances the column when it is below cached line length. Zero also reports uninitialized state, excessive distance or line end; line end itself changes the cursor toward a newer line.')
change('hsd_80394068','state_behavior','Returns zero unchanged when uninitialized or unsigned distance > capacity, independently of capture enable. Equality to capacity is not rejected. Below cached line length, returns the buffered byte and increments column even if that byte is NUL. At line end returns zero, calls hsd_80393EF4(0, -1), then resets column to zero.')
change('hsd_80394128','data_flow','Converts the signed requested coordinates to hsd_80393E68 unsigned arguments, then reads using the resolved shared column, distance and cached line length if initialized and within the distance bound. An in-line read increments column even for a NUL byte. Debug-console callers use the result to probe text availability and adjust navigation; this accessor changes global cursor state.')
change('hsd_80394128','game_mapping','Supplies text-availability probes to debug-console navigation and periodic row advancement. A memory-dump action probes coordinate 0,0 after enabling capture before emitting report lines. These callers interpret zero as absent text although a stored NUL can also produce zero.')
change('hsd_80394128','inferred_type','Signature u8 (s32 col, s32 row). Coordinates convert to unsigned arguments for absolute seek; the returned byte may be stored text or zero from uninitialized state, excessive distance, line end or stored NUL. It is a mutating seek-and-read operation, not a pure probe.')
change('hsd_80394128','purpose','Seeks the shared report-history cursor to unsigned-converted, column-clamped coordinates and attempts one byte read. Zero indicates several conditions including line end and stored NUL; a beyond-end requested column is clamped rather than rejected as an invalid coordinate.')
change('hsd_80394128','state_behavior','Calls absolute seek first, which leaves state unchanged when uninitialized. Then returns zero for uninitialized state or selected distance > capacity, independently of capture enable. An in-line read advances column even for NUL. At line end returns zero, calls relative movement 0,-1 and resets column. Negative inputs are converted to unsigned seek coordinates rather than explicitly rejected.')
change('hsd_803941E8','data_flow','Calls HSD_VIWaitXFBFlushNoYield and obtains the last-drawn index. If index != -1, writes that buffer through xfb_cur without a NULL check. Scans configured records in index order, skipping that index and stopping each scan at a nonzero buffer; writes up to two primary slots but leaves a slot untouched if its scan visits no eligible record. If primary slot zero is zero, transfers *xfb_cur and clears it when that pointer is non-NULL, otherwise returns zero. The known display initializer zeroes its state before passing the primary and current slots.')
change('hsd_803941E8','game_mapping','Provides framebuffer addresses to the debug-console display initializer, whose zeroed state supplies two primary slots and a current slot. It skips the index returned by the video last-draw helper and can transfer the current slot as fallback. This is not a general validation of framebuffer safety or non-NULL outputs.')
change('hsd_803941E8','inferred_type','Declared s32 (void* xfb_out_ptr, void* xfb_cur_ptr). The first pointer must address two readable/writable 32-bit slots; the second must be writable when last_draw != -1 and is read/write during fallback. Slots can retain caller values when no scan writes them. Return is 0, 1 or 2 by the final branch tests, not a guarantee that this many nonzero distinct buffers were found.')
change('hsd_803941E8','purpose','Waits for the video flush helper, saves the last-drawn buffer when available, and scans for up to two other configured XFB addresses. It can transfer the saved current address into primary slot zero. The wait helper returns immediately with fewer than two configured XFBs; output validity also depends on caller storage initialization.')
change('hsd_803941E8','state_behavior','For >=2 configured XFBs, the wait helper busy-waits while WAITDONE, DRAWDONE or NEXT records remain; for fewer it returns immediately. Selection skips last_draw and starts the second scan after the first stop index. Output slots are not pre-cleared here. A nonnegative last_draw dereferences xfb_cur before the later NULL fallback check. A zero first slot with NULL current pointer returns 0; otherwise returns 2 if slot one is nonzero, else 1, even if fallback transferred zero. The known caller pre-zeroes storage.')
change('FILE','data_flow','Initialization clears the first 0x24 bytes of its 0x28-byte state while preserving x24, stores and zeroes caller-owned storage, and registers fn_80393C14. With stdout interception installed by HSD_LogInit, incoming bytes flow to the ring and length trailers. Seek and read operations maintain a shared history cursor consumed by debug-console drawing and address parsing. The separate XFB helper supplies display-buffer slots.')
change('FILE','state_behavior','The initialized flag x0_b0 gates seek, relative movement and byte reads; x0_b1 separately tracks report capture and disabling capture leaves history readable. The coordinate getter is unconditional. Absolute traversal checks prior distance against capacity and can end beyond it; reads reject distance > capacity. Positive relative movement leaves cached line length unchanged, and zero-row movement is ignored only in the in-range branch. Capture has no zero-capacity guard. Zero read results can also be stored NUL bytes.')
